a `str` is not a collection in Oro — `s.to_list()` is the bridge into the collection protocol, so write `s.to_list().sort_by(x => x)`
a `bytes` is not a collection in Oro — `b.to_list()` is the bridge into the collection protocol, so write `b.to_list().sort_by(x => x)`
`len` is a builtin in Oro and not a method on `str`/`bytes` — write `len(s)`
